eatedAt=2026-07-23T21:54:45.108455, deletedAt=null, rejectReason=null), DocumentResponse(id=a84e5bdb-192c-4ec3-93e7-0dc53b5629ee, ownerId=2c0933a6-63db-4e9e-8848-66fc2b5de9d9, folderId=e719ae0c-cbc6-423f-a7e3-b3c989425cb4, subjectId=13411a98-f6ca-4213-bfa3-ab978db52534, title=2, description=null, summary=# English Grammar Summary for Medical Students

This guide covers essential grammar rules for clinical reporting, descriptive comparisons, and language structure.

---

### 1. Reported Speech
Used to convey what someone else said. When the reporting verb is in the **past**, you must:
*   **Backshift tenses:** (e.g., Present Simple $\rightarrow$ Past Simple; Past Simple $\rightarrow$ Past Perfect).
*   **Change pronouns:** (e.g., "I" $\rightarrow$ "He/She").
*   **Adjust time/place words:** 
    *   *Now* $\rightarrow$ *Then*
    *   *Yesterday* $\rightarrow$ *The day before*
    *   *Today* $\rightarrow$ *That day*

---

### 2. Agreement (So / Too / Neither / Either)
Used to show agreement with a statement.

| Agreement | Structure | Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Positive (So)** | So + aux + subject | ...and **so am I.** |
| **Positive (Too)** | Subject + aux + too | ...and **I am too.** |
| **Negative (Neither)** | Neither + aux + subject | ...and **neither do I.** |
| **Negative (Either)** | Subject + aux + either | ...and **I don't either.** |

---

### 3. Comparison
Used to evaluate medical conditions or treatment efficacy.

*   **Comparative:** Short adj + *er* / *more* + long adj + *than*.
*   **Superlative:** *The* + short adj + *est* / *the most* + long adj.
*   **Equal:** *as + adj + as*.
*   **Irregular Forms:**
    *   Good $\rightarrow$ Better $\rightarrow$ Best
    *   Bad $\rightarrow$ Worse $\rightarrow$ Worst
    *   Far $\rightarrow$ Farther/Further $\rightarrow$ Farthest/Furthest

---

### 4. Word Forms (Suffixes)
Recognizing word parts helps identify the function of vocabulary in medical texts.

*   **Noun (-tion, -sion, -ment, -ness, -ity, -er, -or, -ism):** *Infection, diagnosis, treatment.*
*   **Verb (-ate, -en, -ify, -ize):** *Vaccinate, strengthen, classify.*
*   **Adjective (-al, -ic, -ive, -ous, -able, -ible):** *Clinical, toxic, effective, nervous.*
*   **Adverb (-ly):** *Normally, quickly.*

---

### 5. Quick Practice Tips
*   **Reported Speech:** Always check if the tense needs to shift before writing your answer.
*   **Agreement:** Match the auxiliary verb to the tense of the original sentence (e.g., use *do/does* for Present Simple, *am/is/are* for "to be").
*   **Comparison:** Ensure you use "than" for comparatives and "the" for superlatives., status=READY, aiStatus=COMPLETED, mimeType=application/pdf, fileSize=4660, cloudinaryUrl=https://res.cloudinary.com/dpx7mzzv1/image/upload/v1784316388/english_grammar_medical.pdf, createdAt=2026-07-23T21:52:14.151610, deletedAt=null, rejectReason=null), DocumentResponse(id=a0a694d0-1e3b-4a46-9214-0af0f8681814, ownerId=2c0933a6-63db-4e9e-8848-66fc2b5de9d9, folderId=e719ae0c-cbc6-423f-a7e3-b3c989425cb4, subjectId=13411a98-f6ca-4213-bfa3-ab978db52534, title=43, description=null, summary=null, status=READY, aiStatus=NOT_STARTED, mimeType=application/pdf, fileSize=30626, cloudinaryUrl=https://res.cloudinary.com/dpx7mzzv1/image/upload/v1784693133/english.pdf, createdAt=2026-07-22T11:05:33.199712, deletedAt=null, rejectReason=null), DocumentResponse(id=71172944-9553-45f4-a11f-ef3af888bee9, ownerId=2c0933a6-63db-4e9e-8848-66fc2b5de9d9, folderId=e719ae0c-cbc6-423f-a7e3-b3c989425cb4, subjectId=13411a98-f6ca-4213-bfa3-ab978db52534, title=1234, description=123, summary=null, status=REPORTED, aiStatus=COMPLETED, mimeType=application/pdf, fileSize=30626, cloudinaryUrl=null, createdAt=2026-07-22T00:52:05.066572, deletedAt=null, rejectReason=null), DocumentResponse(id=e32ff6f4-07ac-445a-9b9e-8b43318fc1d7, ownerId=2c0933a6-63db-4e9e-8848-66fc2b5de9d9, folderId=e719ae0c-cbc6-423f-a7e3-b3c989425cb4, subjectId=13411a98-f6ca-4213-bfa3-ab978db52534, title=1, description=null, summary=# Tóm tắt Ngữ pháp Tiếng Anh trọng tâm

## 1. Reported Speech (Câu tường thuật)
Dùng để thuật lại lời nói của người khác. Khi động từ tường thuật ở quá khứ (*said, told*), cần thực hiện 3 thay đổi:
*   **Đổi đại từ:** (I → he/she; my → his/her...).
*   **Đổi thời gian/nơi chốn:** (now → then; today → that day; yesterday → the day before...).
*   **Lùi thì:**
    *   Hiện tại đơn → Quá khứ đơn
    *   Hiện tại tiếp diễn → Quá khứ tiếp diễn
    *   Hiện tại hoàn thành → Quá khứ hoàn thành
    *   Quá khứ đơn → Quá khứ hoàn thành
    *   *Will → Would, Can → Could, Must → Had to*

## 2. So / Too / Neither / Either
Dùng để đồng tình với ý kiến của người khác:
*   **Khẳng định ("Cũng vậy"):**
    *   *So + trợ động từ + S*
    *   *S + trợ động từ + too*
    *   Ví dụ: "I'm happy." → "So am I" hoặc "I am too."
*   **Phủ định ("Cũng không"):**
    *   *Neither + trợ động từ + S*
    *   *S + trợ động từ + either*
    *   Ví dụ: "I don't know." → "Neither do I" hoặc "I don't either."

## 3. Comparison (So sánh)
| Loại so sánh | Cấu trúc (Ngắn / Dài) |
| :--- | :--- |
| **So sánh hơn** | adj-er + than / more + adj + than |
| **So sánh nhất** | the + adj-est / the most + adj |
| **So sánh bằng** | as + adj + as |

*   **Lưu ý tính từ bất quy tắc:**
    *   Good → Better → Best
    *   Bad → Worse → Worst
    *   Many/Much → More → Most

## 4. Word Forms (Nhận biết loại từ)
Cách nhận biết từ loại thông qua hậu tố:
*   **Danh từ (Noun):** -tion, -sion, -ment, -ness, -ity, -er, -or, -ism.
*   **Động từ (Verb):** -ate, -en, -ify, -ize.
*   **Tính từ (Adjective):** -al, -ic, -ive, -ous, -able, -ible.
*   **Trạng từ (Adverb):** -ly (thường bổ nghĩa cho động từ)., status=READY, aiStatus=COMPLETED, mimeType=application/pdf, fileSize=30626, cloudinaryUrl=https://res.cloudinary.com/dpx7mzzv1/image/upload/v1784335142/english.pdf, createdAt=2026-07-21T20:31:34.064794, deletedAt=null, rejectReason=null)])]
